cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite the associated paper.
title: "Code and Text-Free Data for Organisation-Level Semantic Identity in K-pop"
authors:
  - family-names: Murali Krishna
    given-names: Brinda
  - family-names: Karakuş
    given-names: Oktay
  - family-names: Eyüpoğlu
    given-names: Can
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oktaykarakus/kpop-company-semantic-identity"
abstract: >-
  Analysis and figure scripts, a text-free song-level dataset (1,289 songs,
  126 artists, four companies, 1997-2023) and numeric result tables supporting
  a computational framework for organisation-level semantic identity. The MIT
  licence covers the code only. The package contains no lyrics and is not a
  complete end-to-end reproduction archive.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "A Computational Framework for Modelling Organisation-Level Semantic Identity from Longitudinal Textual Data"
